//RS mod jet_gtk {
//RS     // I1 containment: every raw C-ABI call in this module is the vetted
//RS     // platform-FFI boundary, audited here and confined here. `tests/golden.rs`
//RS     // strips this whole `mod jet_gtk { … }` before asserting generated Rust is
//RS     // free of the low-level tier keyword — the same treatment the S58 C-FFI
//RS     // wrapper modules (`user___c_*`), `jet_mem`, and the POSIX term shims get.
//RS     // The loader below uses `dlopen`/`dlsym`, so ordinary programs do not
//RS     // link-load GTK. Native GTK is opened only when this backend is used and
//RS     // the display path is initialized.
//RS     //
//RS     // Retained-mode widget model: canonical `JetUiNode` trees reconcile by stable
//RS     // path into real GtkBox/GtkLabel/GtkButton/GtkEntry widgets. Repaint updates
//RS     // those widgets in place and removes stale children. The existing handle event
//RS     // methods bind those reconciled widgets rather than creating a second tree.
//RS     //
//RS     // Headless safety: with `JET_UI_HEADLESS=1` or no display, `gtk_init_check`
//RS     // is false, no widgets are created, and every op is a safe no-op — the
//RS     // program still runs (signals update, terminal output prints) and
//RS     // terminates, so tests are deterministic and a display-less CI never hangs.
